# cw101, the deckhand without a deck (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw101
revision 1
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent none
tier standard
written_for cty_dray_merewell
written_by claude-p11-pilot
title the deckhand without a deck
fits stage=adult|old
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk sleeps_badly_before_storms
likes fried_fish long_walks market_bustle warm_rain
dislikes flies smoke
fears storms_that_wont_break
hopes a_boat_of_his_own
topics work +0.4 dreams +0.3 weather +0.3 food +0.2 faith -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=short tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# hauls and coils at a boat shed with no boat to speak of: plain, short of temper, reserved, hungry to make a name, and he never sleeps the night before a storm.

words
oath! = Rope and rudder | Blast the sky
saying! = A rope's only as good as the paw on it | You don't get a boat by wishing at the water
weather = weather coming | a blow on the way
nowink = not a wink | two hours, if that
grandad = my grandad's old boat | the boat my grandad had
fried = fish fried in butter | a bit of fish done in butter
walk = a long walk with nowhere to be | a walk out past the walls
roar = the market at its busiest | the market at full roar
lake = Glasswater | the big lake I grew up on
hull = a hull with my name painted on | a boat with my name on it
before = three of us before me | my grandad and his father before him
hauling = hauling and coiling | scraping hulls that aren't mine
reek = smoke off the works | that smokehouse reek
copper = a handful of copper | not much copper
flies = flies on the fish | flies in summer
rope = rope that goes nowhere | rope for a boat that isn't there
door = the shed door | the door of the shed
roof = a roof that doesn't leak | a better roof than this one
yard = every House yard on the Wharf | every yard with a House name over the gate

grown
scene cant_sleep
when topic=weather|health here.weather=overcast|storm
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : #weather.capitalize#. I'll get #nowink# tonight. | I lay awake till the bells. There's #weather#, and my fur knows it before the sky does. | Feel that? Heavy. I'll get #nowink# till it breaks.
b : How can you tell? | Every time? | Can't you just sleep?
a : The air goes thick and sounds carry. #weather.capitalize#, it says. | Every time since I was a pup. #oath#, I'd trade it for a night's sleep. | No. I lie in #bed# listening for it.
b : Strange gift. | Rough on you. | Then I hope it breaks soon.

scene storm_broke
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : It's broken, at least. I'll sleep through the rest like a #child#. | Waiting's the worst of it. #weather.capitalize# I can't stand; the storm itself I can. | #oath#. Listen to it. And I was up all night waiting for it to start.
b : That's backwards. | Funny way round. | You'll sleep tonight, then.
a : I know it is. #oath#, that's how I'm made. | Maybe. It's the not knowing. #bad.capitalize#, every time. | Like the dead, once it's done. #bc_i_hope_so#

scene warm_rain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain here.season=spring|summer
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Warm rain. Best weather there is. I'll walk home in it. | A warm rain after a dry week. The whole street smells like it's been washed, #oath#. | I stood out in it on my break. Couldn't help it.
b : Rather you than me. | It does, a bit. | On purpose?
a : Suit yourself. I'll be the one in a #good# mood. | Smoke's knocked down, for once. #good.capitalize#. | On purpose. #bc_every_time#

scene shed_no_boat
when topic=work self.job=sailor|fisher|none self.workplace
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : A deckhand at #self.workplace#, and no boat to speak of. I coil #rope#. | #hauling.capitalize#. That's my trade now. | They pay me #copper# to keep the place ready for a boat that's never coming.
b : It's work. | That's a trade, sort of. | Somebody's paying, at least.
a : It's #work#. It's not the work. | It's a trade for now. Not for long, if I've my way. #saying.capitalize#. | Somebody's paying #copper#. I'll take it and keep looking.

scene shed_waiting
when topic=work self.workplace
does tell.complaint / sympathise / assess
a : Half my day's waiting for #boss# to tell me what to do. I'd sooner be told wrong than not at all. | Stood at #door# three hours today. Nothing came in. | I asked #boss# for more work again. Got told to wait again.
b : Waiting's the worst. | That's a long three hours. | They'll come round.
a : It is. I'm #bad# at it, and I know it. | Long enough to count every gull on the roof. Twice, #oath#. | Maybe. I'll ask again tomorrow, and the day after. #saying.capitalize#.

scene three_watching
when topic=work|family self.from=coldwater
does confide / react.self / assess
a : #before.capitalize#, all on the water. I feel them watching me coil rope in a shed. | #grandad.capitalize# would've had words for this job. None of them kind. | I'm the third one to carry the trade, and the first with no boat. That sits on me.
b : They'd understand. | He'd have had words for anything. | It's not your doing.
a : Maybe. #mum.capitalize# would still expect better. So do I. | He would. #grandad.capitalize# was right more than wrong. | No. But it's mine to fix. #saying.capitalize#.

scene own_boat
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.plan / answer.plan / assess
a : I'll have #hull# by thirty. You watch. | I'm putting by #copper# a week for a boat. A little one. It's a start. | #someday.capitalize# I'll be the one hiring. Not standing at the door waiting to be hired.
b : How will you manage it? | How much have you got? | Good luck to you.
a : Work, and saving, and not letting anybody talk me out of #hull#. | #copper.capitalize#. It'll be more. | I don't need #luck#. I need a chance.
b : I believe you. | It's a start. | Then I hope you get one.

scene name_made
when topic=dreams|times self.age<=35
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Folk my age are waiting for something to happen. I'm working for #hull#. | I'll not be #hauling# at forty. Not at thirty, either. | Every wolf on the Wharf knows a captain's name. One day they'll know mine.
b : Big plans. | Steady on. | That's a lot to want.
a : They're the only kind worth having. | I've been steady. Steady's got me #copper# and a shed. | It's not too much. It's what's owed to the ones before me, #oath#.

scene fried_fish
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #fried.capitalize#, and I'm a happy wolf. Nothing else does it. | Somebody on the Wharf was frying fish at noon. I nearly gave them my day's #wages# for it. | Plain fish, a hot pan, butter. That's #fried#. Folk ruin it with sauces.
b : Sounds good. | Nearly? | What's wrong with a sauce?
a : It is. Better than anything #toffs# eat up the hill. | Nearly. #copper.capitalize# is all I had. | Hides the fish. If you're hiding it, it's a #bad# fish.

scene long_walk
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Day off, and I'll take #walk#. Clears my head. | I took #walk# on my rest day. Didn't stop till the road ran out. | When I'm angry I walk. I walked #far# last week.
b : Where to? | That far? | What were you angry at?
a : Nowhere. That's the point of #walk#. | #far.capitalize#. My legs thanked me, after. | The usual. Waiting. #reek#. Doesn't matter now.

scene market_roar
when topic=smalltalk|pastimes here.region=ridgemere
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I like #roar#. Everybody shouting, everything moving. | #roar.capitalize# at noon. That's the only time the city feels awake. | Noise never bothered me. Give me #roar# over a quiet street.
b : I can't stand it. | Too loud for me. | Quiet's restful.
a : Then go early. Leave #roar# to me. | Loud's alive. #bc_it_is# | Not for me. Quiet's where I start thinking about #hull#.

scene the_reek
when topic=smalltalk|health here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #reek.capitalize#. It's in my fur, my food, my bed. | I can't breathe on the low streets for #reek#. | Smoke's the worst thing about the city. Worse than the prices, and that's saying something.
b : You get used to it. | It's bad today. | Worse than the prices?
a : I won't. I've tried, #oath#. | It's #bad# every day. Some days it's worse. | Near enough. #money.capitalize# won't buy you out of smoke.

scene flies_fish
when topic=animals|season here.season=summer
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #flies.capitalize#, and more in the shed. Summer's not worth it. | I could do without summer, just for #flies#. | Every fly in the city knows where the Wharf is.
b : They're everywhere. | It's bad this year. | Can't blame them.
a : Everywhere I am, anyway. | It's #bad# every year. | I can. They lay eggs in it.

scene my_spouse
when topic=family|friends self.married=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My #self.spouse_word# thinks I want too much. Maybe I do. I'd rather that than want nothing. | #self.spouse# keeps me honest. Tells me when I'm being short. I'm short a lot. | I'd like to give #self.spouse# #roof#. I will.
b : Wanting's not bad. | That's worth having. | You will, then.
a : No. It's only hard to live beside. | #bc_it_is# I don't say so often enough. | I said I will. #oath#, I meant it.

scene rooms_rise
when topic=home here.region=ridgemere self.from=coldwater
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Two rooms in the Commons and a leak by the window. Not forever; I'll get #roof#. | Our rooms are fine. Small. The stair's steep. I don't complain about it. | We've a window that looks at a wall. I want one that looks at water, like #lake#.
b : It never is. | You just did. | Water, eh?
a : No. I'll see to that, #oath#. | Fair. I'm short with everything; the stair's no different. | Water. I grew up on #lake#. A wall's no view.

scene lake_back_home
when topic=memories|travel self.from=coldwater self.away=yes
does tell.memory / react.story / assess
a : On #lake# you could see a storm come across the water an hour off. Here it comes over the roofs with no warning. | I miss #lake# on a flat morning. Every boat out, every sound carrying. | I learned to row before I could tie a knot. #grandad.capitalize# said that was the wrong way round.
b[from=coldwater] #lake : An hour, and you could still get in. | Nothing like it. | He was right.
b : Do you go back? | Sounds peaceful. | Was it?
a@lake : If you were quick. I was always quick. | Nothing. The Sound's a different animal. | He usually was. I never told him so.
a : Not yet. Not till I've #hull# to show for it. | #bc_it_was# I didn't know it then. | Probably. I'd row first again, knots or no knots.

scene bread_up
when topic=prices world.bread_price=up
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Bread's up again. Nothing coming into my house, and still they put it up. #robbery#. | Bread's dearer. I'd like to know who's getting the #money#. | They've put the loaf up. I'll eat less of it and go #hungry#. That's all I can do.
b[role=merchant] #trade : It's the flour. | Not us. We pay more too. | It'll come down.
b : It always is. | Not you, anyway. | That's no answer.
a@trade : There's always something. It's never the one selling. | Then who? Somebody's doing well out of it. | Maybe. I'll not hold my breath.
a : It is. #bad.capitalize#, the whole business. | No. Not me. I'm #skint#. | It's the only answer there is, #oath#.

scene empty_bench
when topic=times|work here.region=ridgemere
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : The Houses would sooner leave a bench empty than take on the likes of me. | I've asked at #yard#. Same answer every time. | They want somebody who's done it before. How do you do it before if nobody lets you?
b[wealth=rich] #rich : They've their reasons. | Keep asking. | Experience counts.
b : That's how it goes. | Every time? | Fair point.
a@rich : I'm sure they do. None of them are mine. | I will. Till they're sick of my face. | It does. Somebody has to give it first.
a : It's how it goes for us. Not for #toffs#. | Every one. #oath#. | I've asked #boss# that. No answer.

scene sermons_no
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I've nothing against the Bright One. It's the plate going round I can't stand. | Praying never got me a day's #wages#. Asking did. | I'll go in for a wedding or a burial. That's my share.
b[job=priest] #priest : The plate keeps the roof up. | Maybe both helped. | Come more often.
b : Fair enough. | Can't argue with that. | That's most of us.
a@priest : Then put it to the Houses. They've more than I have. | Maybe. I'll take credit for the asking. | I'll come when I've something to give. Not before.
a : #bc_fair_enough# | No. Try, though, and see what #money# it gets you. | #bc_it_is# And that's enough.

scene new_faces
when topic=newcomer
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Every new face is another wolf after the same scraps of #work# I am. | I've nothing against them. I just got here first. | More come every month. The #work# doesn't grow.
b : They've to eat too. | Fair enough. | It's hard on everyone.
a : I know it. I'd still rather they ate somewhere else. | I'll not be short with them for it. Not unless they're short first. | It is. #bc_it_is#

scene the_dole
when topic=times self.on_dole=yes
does confide / react.self / assess
a : There's weeks #copper# from the parish is the only bread we see. I don't like saying it. | I take #dole#. No pride in it, and no shame either. | #someday.capitalize# I'll pay back every loaf. In #money#, or in hiring.
b : No shame in it. | Good. | You will.
a : #bc_i_know# I still don't like it. | It's a step. Steps get you up. | I will. #saying.capitalize#.

story the_grandad_boat [concept=talk.memories self.from=coldwater]
  : My grandad had a boat on #lake#. Flat-bottomed, tarred black, older than he was.
  : When it went, it went to pay a debt. Nobody in the family's had one since.
  ask : Is that why you want one?
  b : Makes sense.
  : I want one because it's ours. #grandad.capitalize# should never have let it go.

story the_night_it_broke [concept=talk.memories self.age>=20]
  : When I was a pup, a storm sat over the town three days and never broke. Nobody slept.
  : The fourth night it came down all at once. Took two roofs and a jetty.
  b : And you've not slept before one since.
  : Not properly. #oath#, I'd give a lot to.

story the_first_day [concept=talk.work self.workplace]
  : My first day at #self.workplace#, I asked where the boat was.
  : They laughed. Said I'd see it when I'd earned my #wages#.
  ask : Have you seen it yet?
  b : Not yet?
  : Not yet. I've earned it twice over. #bc_we_will_see#

opinion @1 houses against 2 : They'd sooner leave a bench empty than take on the likes of me. I've stood at #yard# to prove it.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : Nothing more coming in, and the prices keep going up. Somebody's doing well out of it, and it's not me. #robbery#.
opinion @1 times against 2 : It gets a bit harder every week, and nobody up the hill notices. #bad.capitalize#, and getting worse.
opinion @1 church against 1 : Praying never once got me #work#. The plate goes round faster than any help does.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : They take what little #work# there is going. I don't blame them for wanting it; I just want it more.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : There are weeks it's the only bread on my table. I'll not hear a word against it, #oath#.
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. | #greet#. You after something?
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Busy. Say it quick. | #greet#. Mind the rope.
line @3 greet [here.weather=overcast|storm] : #greet#. #weather.capitalize#. | #greet#. Don't ask how I slept.
line @1 again.open : You again. #greet#. | Back already? #greet#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : #greet#. Eaten yet? | There you are. #greet#.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. What is it?
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family|spouses] : #greet#. Good to see a face I know. | #greet#. Sit, if you want.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the weather.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, then.
line @1 react.news.new : #oath#. That's news. | #surprise#. When was that?
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. Everyone's heard. | #knew#. It was round the Wharf by noon.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. I'll believe it when I see it. | I'd not take that as fact till somebody who saw it says so.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. That's a bad thing. | #oath#. I'm sorry to hear it.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. Slept badly. | Well enough. #busy.capitalize#, or I'd like to be. | #tired.capitalize#. #weather.capitalize#.
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. If there's something I can do, say so. | That's rough, #address#. I mean it.
line @1 decline : No. I can't spare it, and I'll not pretend I can. | #refuse#. I've nothing to give this week, and that's the truth.
line @1 accept_decline : Fine. #later.capitalize#, then. | #no_matter#.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. | #thanks#. I'll pay it back.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It's nothing, #address#. | #deflect#.
line @1 preclose : Right. #excuse#. | #preclose#.
line @1 ack : Right. | #ack#.
line @1 insist : #insist#. I'll not change my mind. | I said what I said.
rule @rope
when concept=bark working=yes self.workplace
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Coil it right or do it again. | #saying.capitalize#.

rule @weather
when concept=bark working=no here.weather=overcast|storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #weather.capitalize#. I'll get #nowink#. | Put the lamp out. I want to hear #weather#.

rule @reek
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #reek.capitalize#. Again. | Can't breathe for #reek#.

rule @roar
when concept=bark here.place=market
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That's more like it. Noise and #money#. | #roar.capitalize#. Good.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : #greet#. You want something, or just passing? | #greet#. I've not much time. What is it?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Out for a walk, or out for work?
dlg @1 resident.job : #self.trade_words#. #hauling.capitalize#. It's work, for now. | #job_busy#
dlg @1 resident.news : Nothing worth repeating. #weather.capitalize#, maybe. | #news_none#
dlg @1 resident.gossip : I don't trade in talk, #address#. Ask somebody with time for it. | #gossip_none#
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the weather.
graft resident.hub
choice You look tired. Bad night? -> night
node night
say #weather.capitalize#. I never sleep before a storm. Never have. I lie there listening for it to break.
mood stern
free
choice Is there nothing that helps? -> night_help
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node night_help
say A long walk the day before. Sometimes. Mostly I just wait it out. #saying.capitalize#, and a storm's no different.
choice I hope it breaks soon. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
